# Family Portal environment.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. The app loads .env from the working directory in
# local builds and /srv/apps/family/shared/.env in release builds (app.go).
# Never commit a filled-in copy — .env is gitignored, this file is not, so the
# values below are placeholders and descriptions only.
#
# "Required" means a release build refuses to start without it
# (backend/config_check.go). Local builds log the same list and keep going, so
# a development machine can run with only what it actually needs.

# --- Required in release ------------------------------------------------

# Public origin, scheme and host only: no trailing slash, no path, https.
# Used to build OAuth redirects, password-reset links, and WebSocket origin
# checks — pointing this at the wrong host sends users returning from Google
# to somewhere that isn't the site.
SITE_ROOT=https://example.com

# Signing key for session JWTs. At least 32 characters, random, not reused
# anywhere else. Changing it invalidates every issued token. Local builds
# generate a throwaway key at startup when this is unset.
JWT_SECRET_KEY=

# Google OAuth web credential. The login page offers "Sign in with Google"
# unconditionally, so a missing credential is a dead button, not a hidden
# feature. Register the redirect URI as $SITE_ROOT/api/google/callback.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Outbound mail. Password reset is the only way a locked-out user gets back in
# without an admin, and the backup staleness alert is the only warning that
# backups stopped, so unconfigured mail loses two release guarantees quietly.
# Two arrangements work:
#   1. MAIL_FROM alone — relayed as that address through a local MTA that
#      authenticates nothing (defaults to 127.0.0.1:25).
#   2. EMAIL + APP_PASSWORD — authenticated submission, sent as EMAIL
#      (defaults to smtp.gmail.com:587).
MAIL_FROM=family@example.com
EMAIL=
APP_PASSWORD=

# Shared secret guarding the database snapshot endpoint the nightly backup
# pulls from (/internal/snapshot). At least 32 characters. Unset in a release
# build is a backup that silently never runs; see docs/restore.md.
BACKUP_TOKEN=

# --- Optional -----------------------------------------------------------

# SMTP host and port. Only needed to override the defaults chosen above.
#SMTP_HOST=
#SMTP_PORT=

# Gemini API key. No feature calls the AI client today - the client in
# backend/ai.go is kept for a future one. Leave unset until something uses it.
#GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Google OAuth client for the iOS companion app (1.1). Optional in 1.0.
#GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=

# Set to any non-empty value to disable rate limiting. Honored only in local
# builds — for load testing and end-to-end runs. A release build always limits.
#RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=

# --- APNs (companion app, 1.1) ------------------------------------------
#
# All-or-nothing: leaving every variable unset is the expected 1.0 state, but
# setting some of them fails startup. A partially configured subsystem looks
# enabled and behaves like it is broken, and it fails where nobody sees it —
# in a device registration. On the production host these are managed by the
# family-apns helper rather than by hand.
#
#APNS_TEAM_ID=
#APNS_KEY_ID=
#APNS_BUNDLE_ID=
#APNS_KEY_PATH=/srv/apps/family/shared/apns/AuthKey.p8
#APNS_ENVIRONMENT=production   # "sandbox" or "production"

# --- Universal links (companion app, 1.1) -------------------------------
#
# <TeamID>.<BundleID> for the iOS app. Set it and the server publishes
# /.well-known/apple-app-site-association, which is what lets a tapped push
# notification — and any familyrecord.app link — open the app instead of
# Safari. Leave it unset and that file 404s, which is the correct answer for a
# server with no app in the field.
#
# Optional, but validated: a malformed value fails startup rather than
# publishing an association naming the wrong app. Apple's CDN and every device
# that installed the app cache this file, so a typo here outlives the deploy
# that fixes it.
#
#IOS_APP_ID=ABCDE12345.app.familyrecord.ios

# --- Face analysis daemon (cmd/faceanalysis, release hosts only) --------
#
# Read by the daemon process, not by the web app. Each has a matching flag.
#
#FACE_SOCKET=/run/family-face/face.sock
#FACE_MODELS=/srv/apps/family/shared/models
#PORT=                          # optional TCP port for the daemon's healthz
